PROMPT 7 — ROUTELESS OFFLINE-FIRST PWA
ROLE

Act as a senior PWA architect and offline systems engineer.

Continue the existing ROUTELESS project.

OBJECTIVE

Make ROUTELESS usable during weak connectivity and complete internet disconnection.

TECHNOLOGIES
React PWA.
Service Workers.
IndexedDB.
Workbox.
Dexie.
Background Sync where supported.
OFFLINE STORAGE

Cache and store:

Application shell.
Bus records.
Stops.
Routes.
Timetables.
Student saved journeys.
Alternative routes.
Last-known bus status.
Last-known GPS.
Emergency transportation plans.
OFFLINE FEATURES

Students must be able to:

Open the installed application.
Search saved destinations.
View saved bus schedules.
Calculate alternative journeys.
View saved emergency instructions.

Drivers must be able to:

Record bus status.
Queue journey updates.
Save GPS records.
Synchronize later.

Kiosks must be able to:

Open without internet.
Search saved routes.
Display cached bus information.
Show the last synchronization time.
SYNCHRONIZATION

Implement:

Local outbox.
Unique operation IDs.
Original timestamps.
Retry handling.
Duplicate prevention.
Resumable synchronization.
Conflict handling.
Synchronization status.

Never claim that an offline update has reached another device.

NETWORK MODES
FULL CONNECTIVITY.
LOW DATA.
OFFLINE.

Display freshness warnings and app version.

ACCEPTANCE TESTS
App opens offline after installation.
Saved routes work offline.
Data survives application restart.
Queued updates synchronize later.
Duplicate uploads are prevented.
Offline status is visible.
Stale information is never hidden.

Demonstrate offline behavior using browser network throttling and airplane mode where supported.

Preserve earlier functionality.
